    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm looking at a 2022 F-150 in the shop. Customer is complaining about the transmission slipping under load. I've got the scan tool hooked up and I'm seeing some really weird irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit during the shifts. What are the most likely things causing these kinds of pressure fluctuations in a modern automatic like this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit could be caused by various issues in the transmission. It's possible there is an issue with the transmission control module receiving incorrect data from the sensors, the hydraulic fluid might be contaminated causing blockages or improper operation, or there could be issues with the solenoids or valves within the transmission. It's also possible that a failing torque converter could be the source of these irregularities. It would be wise to check the service and filter replace if needed and consider conducting a pressure test and inspection of the electronic components for precise diagnosis.",
